{"Provider Method Contract Breaks: When the source integration differs from the linked issue's integration, the task calls sync_assignee_outbound with a new assignment_source keyword, but provider implementations with the previous (external_issue, user, assign=...) signature will raise TypeError, causing the Celery task to retry and then drop the assignee sync": 0.5936992168426514, "Same-Integration Links Are Suppressed: The check suppresses by integration id only, so if a Sentry issue is linked to two external issues in the same Jira integration and one webhook changes the assignee, the outbound pass skips the other linked Jira issue, leaving it with a stale assignee": 0.81085205078125, "Malformed Source Fails Open: When a queued task receives a malformed or version-mismatched assignment_source_dict, from_dict returns None, and the task treats it the same as a local Sentry assignment, skipping the cycle-prevention check and potentially syncing the assignment back to the integration that produced the webhook": 0.7757503390312195}